     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block h1_2:escalate and h1_1:access. No single block is enough. crown:obtain is an OR of h5_1, h5_0 and h5_2. Blocking h1_2 kills h3_2 and h2_1. Losing h2_1 kills h3_1, and with h3_2 also gone, h4_1 and h5_0 die. h5_2 is an AND that needs h3_2, so it dies too. h5_1 is still reachable through h3_0, which comes from h1_1 (an AND of edge0 and edge1, both entry footholds). Blocking h1_1 closes that last path. For a single block: h5_1 can be reached via h3_2 or via h3_0, and h3_0 depends only on h1_1. No one step lies on both of those routes, so one block cannot work.\"}\n```"
